	"title" "More Network Capacity Renew by NgocDuy"
	"description" "[h1]✨ WHAT'S NEW (v3.4 Hotfix: Phantom CitizenUnits & Simulation Optimization) ✨[/h1]
[list]
[*] [b]Phantom CitizenUnits Auto-Sanitization & Lag Fix:[/b]
[list]
    [*] Permanently eliminated the issue where 'Phantom CitizenUnits' accumulated up to 1,000+ (detected by Phantom Lane Remover and similar diagnostic tools), preventing simulation lag and memory bloat.
    [*] Added a built-in high-performance [b]CitizenUnit Auto-Sanitizer[/b] running on level load and pre-save that detects and safely purges orphaned CitizenUnits and cleans dangling home/work/vehicle pointers down to [b]0 phantom units[/b].
    [*] Building sanitization now properly releases attached citizen units before flag reset, preventing custom building assets from orphaning citizens.
    [*] Hotkey support: Press [b]Ctrl + Shift + C[/b] (or [b]Cmd + Shift + C[/b] on Mac) anytime during gameplay to trigger an instant on-demand CitizenUnits sanitization!
[/list]
[*] [b]Isolated Ghost Transit Line Vehicle Cleanup:[/b]
[list]
    [*] Eliminated disruptive city-wide vehicle wipeouts on level load. Deactivating corrupted ghost lines now releases ONLY the vehicles belonging to that specific broken line, preserving all other traffic, emergency vehicles, and passenger cims intact.
    [*] Safely unspawns and resets stuck waiting citizens at transit stops via clean citizen instance recycling.
[/list]
[*] [b]Critical Save Game & SavePanel Stability (v3.3):[/b]
[list]
    [*] Universal pre-save simulation sanitization (SimulationManager & TransportManager) and out-of-bounds safety guards across all PrefabCollection serializers (TransportInfo, VehicleInfo, BuildingInfo, NetInfo).
    [*] Fixed SavePanel UI lockup/freeze upon saving completion, allowing save dialogs to close and reset cleanly.
[/list]
[*] [b]Complete Road & Building Placement Fix:[/b]
[list]
    [*] Permanently resolved the critical vanilla engine limitation where players were unable to draw roads or place buildings once network entities exceeded vanilla limits.
    [*] Automatically expands ToolController collision bitmasks (m_collidingSegments & m_collidingBuildings) to 65,536 bits, eliminating IndexOutOfRangeException crashes in NetTool and BuildingTool when combined with Network Anarchy.
[/list]
[*] [b]Comprehensive 16-Mod Ecosystem Compatibility:[/b]
[list]
    [*] [b]Adaptive Roads (ADR):[/b] Expands and synchronizes all 6 core buffers (NodeBuffer, SegmentBuffer, SegmentEndBuffer 130K, LaneBuffer 524K, m_updatedNodes 1024 longs, m_updatedSegments 1024 longs). Fixes legacy MoreNetworkCapacity crashes at node 65,024 and unallocated LaneBuffer errors.
    [*] [b]Network Skins 2:[/b] Seamlessly scales SegmentSkins (65K) and NodeSkins (65K), preventing skin calculation crashes on extended networks.
    [*] [b]Node Controller Renewal:[/b] Expands NodeData Buffer up to 65K nodes.
    [*] [b]Move It, Picker, Network Multitool, Intersection Marking Tool (IMT):[/b] Dynamic IL Transpilation scales all 32K/36K boundary checks up to 65K.
    [*] [b]Network Anarchy, Advanced Road Tools, Network Extensions 2, Improved Public Transport 2/3, Advanced Vehicle Options:[/b] Fully verified and 100% operational.
[/list]
[*] [b]Savegame & Pathfinding Protection:[/b] Preserves the dedicated SavePanel.OnSavingComplete safety patch (preventing EndOfStreamException save corruptions) and ensures untampered TM:PE CustomPathFind threads for cars, buses, trams, trains, and emergency vehicles.
[/list]

[hr][/hr]

[h1]MORE NETWORK CAPACITY RENEW[/h1]
[b]The Definitive 64K Network Limit Breaker for Cities: Skylines[/b]
[i]Fully rewritten, optimized, and stabilized by NgocDuy[/i]

[hr][/hr]

[h1]WHAT IS THIS MOD?[/h1]
Have you ever hit the infamous [b]'Cannot create more objects of this type'[/b] limit while building your dream metropolis?
Vanilla Cities: Skylines caps your road and transit networks at ~32,000 nodes and segments.

[b]More Network Capacity Renew[/b] safely expands your game internal network limits to [b]65,536 (64K) Nodes and Segments[/b] - giving you double the building freedom!

Unlike unstable or abandoned experimental versions that caused fatal crashes, broken placement tools, and corrupted traffic, [b]Renew[/b] is engineered from the ground up for [b]maximum stability, accurate traffic simulation, and zero data loss.[/b]

[hr][/hr]

[h1]KEY ADVANTAGES & SUPERIOR FEATURES[/h1]
[list]
[*] [b]64K Expanded Capacity:[/b] Doubles the maximum network node and segment limits (up to 65,536) and lanes up to 524,288. Build massive regional transit grids, hyper-detailed highway interchanges, and expansive subway networks without restriction.
[*] [b]Full Road & Building Placement Guarantee:[/b] Solved engine-level ToolController collision bitmask limits, allowing smooth placement of roads, bridges, tunnels, intersections, and buildings without tool lockups.
[*] [b]Native Apple Silicon & Intel Mac Stability:[/b] Fixed deep engine crash loops, memory boundary overflows, and native crashes that plagued previous limit mods on macOS (M1/M2/M3/M4 & Intel).
[*] [b]Complete TM:PE Compatibility:[/b]
[list]
    [*] Timed Traffic Lights (TTL) are 100% operational on expanded nodes (> 32,768).
    [*] Custom lane connections, lane arrows, speed limits, and priority rules are fully respected.
    [*] Node data and timed phases persist cleanly through save/load cycles without missing references.
[/list]
[*] [b]Accurate Traffic Flow & Real-Time Heatmaps:[/b]
[list]
    [*] Full traffic flow color refresh across all extended segments.
    [*] Active simulation loop prevents the notorious 'frozen vehicles' or phantom deadlock bug at high-ID junctions.
[/list]
[*] [b]Safe Persistence Guarantee:[/b] Implements clean savegame serialization to ensure your custom traffic setups, timed nodes, and networks reload perfectly with zero data loss.
[*] [b]Deep 16-Mod Ecosystem Compatibility:[/b] Seamless integration with Adaptive Roads, Network Skins, Node Controller Renewal, Move It, IMT, Network Multitool, Network Anarchy, Picker, Find It, etc.
[/list]

[hr][/hr]

[h1]COMPATIBILITY[/h1]
Tested and fully compatible with the standard modern modding ecosystem:
[list]
[*] [b]Harmony 2.2+[/b] (Required dependency)
[*] [b]TM:PE (Traffic Manager: President Edition)[/b] (STABLE & LABS)
[*] [b]Network Anarchy[/b]
[*] [b]Adaptive Roads (ADR)[/b]
[*] [b]Network Skins 2[/b]
[*] [b]Node Controller Renewal[/b]
[*] [b]Intersection Marking Tool (IMT)[/b]
[*] [b]Network Multitool[/b]
[*] [b]Move It[/b]
[*] [b]Picker[/b]
[*] [b]Find It 2[/b]
[*] [b]81 Tiles 2[/b]
[*] [b]Advanced Road Tools[/b]
[*] [b]Improved Public Transport 2 & 3[/b]
[*] [b]Advanced Vehicle Options[/b]
[*] [b]Train Car Selector[/b]
[/list]

[hr][/hr]

[h1]REQUIREMENTS[/h1]
[list]
[*] [url=https://steamcommunity.com/workshop/filedetails/?id=2040656402]Harmony 2.2.2-0 (CitiesHarmony)[/url]
[/list]

[hr][/hr]

[h1]BEST PRACTICES & RECOMMENDATIONS[/h1]
[list]
[*] [b]Backup Your Saves:[/b] As with any mod altering foundational game limits, always keep regular backup copies of your favorite cities.
[*] [b]Persistent Saves:[/b] Once a city exceeds vanilla network limits (> 32,768 nodes/segments), this mod must remain enabled to load and manage those extended networks properly.
[/list]

[hr][/hr]
[i]Developed with precision and care for the Cities: Skylines community by NgocDuy.[/i]"
	"changenote" "v3.8.3: Precise vehicle state differentiation: Completely eliminated false stops on moving/decelerating cars. Moving vehicles (speed > 0), vehicles stopped at red lights/stop signs, and vehicles queued in traffic jams behind other cars are 100% untouched. Only true 'dead vehicles' (completely motionless for >10s on clear roads with zero obstacles ahead) are unclogged and woken up."
